ion among TP53-intact and KEAP1-intact lines, signed estimate +0.774, interval +0.736 to +0.813, despite a smaller exposed cell_n of 81. These restricted estimates are all far larger than the 10% clinical-significance benchmark and show that the accepted large associations are not simple proxies for one another or limited to lines containing the other major genetic state. They still remain observational cell-line associations, not causal or generalizable claims.

