  "narrative": "H10 response deadline: validation R39 (signed +0.7925, independent interval +0.7627 to +0.8223) closely replicates discovery R10 (signed +0.7840, +0.7646 to +0.8034). Because H10 direction is -1, the raw SMARCA4-loss minus SMARCA4-intact contrast is negative, meaning SMARCA4-loss lines have stronger SMARCA2 dependency. This is decisive and far beyond the practical 0.1 dependency-unit threshold, so H10 remains accepted and closed. H67 validation R65 (signed +0.3288, independent interval +0.2553 to +0.4022) confirms discovery R55 (signed +0.2674, +0.2153 to +0.3195). With direction -1, PTEN-loss lines have a raw negative STAT3 dependency shift, i.e. stronger STAT3 dependency. The effect is robust after validation adjustment and exceeds the clinically meaningful benchmark; I accept H67 and close the direct claim while retaining context tests. With H13, H8, H10, and H67 now validated, the strongest dataset-level evidence supports KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency, SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, and PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency. H7 (TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency) and H94 (CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2 dependency) remain accepted associations, but H7 is unvalidated and H94 is modest (discovery estimate 0.117 with lower bound 0.082) and potentially confounded by TP53 or MTAP co-deletion; therefore the next panel evaluates p53 context, MTAP specificity, screen-quality robustness, and PTEN specificity. Negative controls support specificity: TP53 loss does not appreciably move SMARCA2, RPL11, POLR2A, or MDM2 overall; PIK3CA and MYC do not move STAT3; RB1, CDKN2A, and MYC do not move KIF18A; ERBB2 and KRAS do not move TMED10; KEAP1, SMARCA4, and MSI effects are not broad cell-state shifts in the tested cross-outcome controls; driver-matched oncogene dependencies were largely null. These are dataset-level associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
