  "research_notes": "Current accepted dataset-level/validated set: TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency (validated); KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency (validated); SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency (validated); MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency (validated); PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency (validated; now accepted in TP53-wt, TP53-loss, and high-quality-screen contexts); CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2 dependency (validated). H104 newly accepted: PTEN loss stronger STAT3 dependency in screen_roc_auc>=0.93, +0.244 [0.183,0.305]. No validation requested for H104 to conserve budget; parent H67 already validated.\n\nNew nulls strengthen specificity: TP53 loss not associated with STAT3 (H95); CDKN2A loss not associated with RPL11 (H116); MTAP loss not associated with RPL11 (H126); RB1 loss not associated with WRN (H117); NF1 loss not associated with KRAS (H118); ERBB2 amplification not associated with EGFR dependency (H119). Interaction nulls: ARID1A does not modify SMARCA4-SMARCA2 (H120); SMARCA4 does not modify KEAP1-NFE2L2 (H121); MYC does not modify CDKN2A-MDM2 (H122); STK11 does not support MSI-WRN synergy (H123); STK11 does not support PTEN-STAT3 interaction (H124).\n\nInterpretation rule remains: signed estimate around or above 0.1 with CI excluding zero is practically meaningful for dependency scores; canonical effects ~0.8, moderate accepted effects ~0.1-0.3. Small nulls with tight intervals support specificity. All associations are within this supplied dataset only.\n\nNext likely uses: activate deferred specificity/main-effect tests such as H68 MYC->RPL11, H125 STK11->MDM2, H127 APC->STAT3 if not already tested, or continue focused specificity. Preserve validation requests unless a new primary association appears. Consider possible future context checks only if an interaction or subgroup effect crosses the practical threshold."
